.fill.justify.offset 5.rightmargin 55.pagesize 48.m1 2.m2 1.m3 2.m4 3.ec X.header /Inews/Network/Inews.footer /Page #//Printed (%)/.in +5.define topic.bold.in -5$1 $2 $3 $4 $5.in +5.en.define endtopic.en.define noform.nojustify.nofill.en.define noformend.justify.fill.en.! Manual created with MWB.! END-OF-MACRO.topic NAMEInews - NetNews Management System.endtopic.topic SYNOPSIS.noforminews [-v] [-a] [-g=<grplist>] [-d=<distlist>]       [-e=<days>] [-r]      [-h]      [-c=<ctrlmsg>:<ctrl-opts>].noformend.endtopic.topic DESCRIPTION  Inews is the program which does the whole management on the local newssystem. In normal use it is started without any option and parses theheader, then write the article in the write directory matching the givennewsgroups. A special kind of a message is the control message (refer toRFC1036) where only a few are executed immediately, other are mailed tothe news administrator. To execute these you have to start inews withthe option.bold-ato switch to admin mode. An explaination of the options follows..in +3.bold-a.in +3Runs inews in admin mode to execute all fed control messages..in -3.bold-e=<days>.in +3Starts to delete all article which have been arrived here more than<days> ago. If a list of groups is given, only these groups areaffected..in -3.bold-r.in +3Rebuild the active file, mostly used in combination with `-e' torecollect the articles in each group. If no groups are specified allgroups are updated..in -3.bold-h.in +3Inews adds all missing headerlines in the article and executes inewsrecrusively. This option may be used when writing a new article and feedit incompletely to inews..in -3.bold-v.in +3All logmessages are then also written to stderr..in -3.bold-g=<groups>.in +3This is a list of groups (seperated by commas) where the actual actionmay take place. Mostly used in combination with `-h', `-e' and `-r'..in -3.bold-d=<dist>.in +3This is a list of distributions (seperated by commas) to where themessage should be send. Mostly used with `-h' and `-c' (see below)..in -3.bold-c=<ctrlmsg>.in +3This creates a control message which may change something on the local(and on remote) news systems. The syntax is.ce-c=<ctrlmsg>[:<option>]{ <option>}All in RFC1036 mentioned control messages are availble, only the `ihave'and `sendme' aren't supported. Refer to RFC1036 for details on eachcontrol message..in -6.endtopic.topic CAVEATSInews isn't a complete newssystem, but just a working subset. It istested against BNews 2.11 and seems to work okay. It won't work witholder ANews versions..endtopic.topic BUGSA lot. This is currently a pre release, so *please* mail all found bugsand problems to me, so I can collect it (and if you have fixed theproblem, send me a context diff)..endtopic.topic FILES.noform.noformend/h0/SPOOL/NEWS.in +3Herein all articles are placed in subdirectories..in -3/h0/USR/LIB/NEWS.in +3All configuration files are placed here, these are:.brActive.in +2The active list of newsgroups..in -2Distributions.in +2The default distributions for several newsgroups..in -2Sys.in +2The systems to feed news to..in -2send_uuname.in +2The file to be send on an senduuname control message..in -2logfile.in +2The logfile of news; if not existing, it isn't written..in -5/h0/USR/LIB/NEWS/HISTORY.in +3All arrived article IDs to prevent duplicate articles..in -3.noformend.endtopic.topic SYSINFO.noformNEWS.BATCH,s=/h0/SPOOL/BATCHNEWS.DIR,s=/h0/SPOOL/NEWSNEWS.LIB,s=/h0/USR/LIB/NEWSlck.inews,lhostname,s=<your hostname>hostdomain,s=<your hostdomain>.in +3Refer to source for details..in -3.noformend.endtopic.topic ENVIROMENT.noform.noformendUSER.in +3is used if no other way can be found to get the login nameof an user..in -3NAME.brFULLNAME.in +3is used if no other way can be found to get the fullnameof an user..in -3ORGANIZATION.in +3is used if no other way can be found to get the organizationof an user..in -3.noformend.endtopic.topic SEE ALSOrnews - in this distributionsbatch - in this distributionRFC1036 - found by your newsfeed (hope so).endtopic.topic AUTHOR.in 0.ce 5Ulrich DessauerKerschensteinerstr. 45, D-8034 GermeringVoice: +49 89 8417811E-Mail: ..!{chiuur|doitcr}!nitmar!udud@nitmar.ddt.sub.org.endtopic